<title>
Rear Door Assembly Removal and Installation
</title>
<ptxt>
<intxrefpoff refid = "AENLJA0A9A06008">Rear Door Components</intxrefpoff>
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Removal and installation procedures for rear door assembly basically the same as 
<intxref refid = "AENLJA0A9A06007">Front Door Assembly Removal and Installation</intxref>
. However, note the following points.
</ptxt>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
Removal and installation center pillar trims. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLJA0A9806011"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Removal and installation rear door trim. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLJA0A9506013"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Tighten bolts and nuts to specified torque. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLJA0A9A06008"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
If paint on door hinge bolts is peeled off, be sure to apply paint again to prevent rust.
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Affix rear door protector at position shown in the figure.
</ptxt>
<figure>
